{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica","id":1038545,"title":"Left-Handed and Lex Magica","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-26T13:06:30-08:00","id":1038545,"title":"Left-Handed and Lex Magica","content":"So I have interesting problem \u2013 <b>How to trial Left-Handed mages in Consilium system, based on Lex Magica?</b> My London players helped lately to <i>capture</i> ( not simply kill ) cabal of Scelesti Libertines that summoned powerful Abyssal Being and before this group send out on the city powerful Acamoth that almost drive it insane ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895970-%E2%80%8B-2e-mystery-yellow-sign-hallows-network-corruption-and-abyssal-astral-realm\">King in Yellow</a> ). BUT they did started it out of Obsessions and curiosity of what would seem NOT dangerous Legacy ( <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/25143-children-of-the-stars-aliens-loving-legacy\">Children of the Stars</a> ), and then where overwhelmed by Abyssal entity when they made contact with.<br /> <br /> Tetragrammaton punishments ( see <b>Sanctum &amp; Sigil</b> for this legal system ) seems to not work with this model, as there is not any simple \u2018kill\u2019 punish \u2013 closest is <i>Spiritual Oblivion</i>, but it\u2019s destroys accused soul, letting him live more as soulless. This does not seems right for Scelesti, as Soulless ends mad in the end, just without magic. Also, it\u2019s said to be marked whole Ruling Council for using this horrible and cruel act as declaring weakness of Council or making precedent to go for war with accused ones allies. (Still, I could see Hierach Civitas in London going for this punishment on his paranoia-level of adhering to \u2018older ways\u2019 and disrespect for Free Council mages.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, less potent punish - <i>Spiritual Scourging</i> \u2013 is sending soul of accused to some far away realm. This would seem as <u>reward</u> for Scelesti, when they <i>can</i> get back their souls if their dedicated enough and start to summon Abyss once more, restarting the cycle.<br /> <br /> In this example, even \u2018kill\u2019 punishment seems not right, as it simply ends life of Scelesti. They cannot fix nothing, they will not change in any other way and more probable than not \u2013 their released souls will make Abyss stronger.<br /> <br /> So my questions are simple \u2013 <b>How you, as Ruling Council, would punish Scelesti</b>? Knowing they were half-aware what they were doing? <b>And do effective killing of accused is practiced punishment in Pentacle society?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-26-2017, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T13:13:30-08:00","id":1038549,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a capital offense to me, especially in London which is a Gaurdian stronghold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T13:31:09-08:00","id":1038553,"title":"","content":"Capital punishment, surely. That's what Interfectors are for. Frankly I'm surprised the Scelesti made it to trial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T16:08:18-08:00","id":1038629,"title":"","content":"Off with their heads!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T20:50:38-08:00","id":1038742,"title":"","content":"The game as written seems limited to exile or execution, but if you want nothing says your table can't have a different answer.<br /> \u200bSend them to Tokyo and park their butts in an Ansho.<br /> \u200bDeath of Personality, use a secret Mind ritual to strip out the parts of their personalities the Pentacle finds unacceptable.<br /> \u200bAn Artifact or device that allows you to lock away the part of their soul that connects to the Supernal without completely severing its link to the individual and leaving them soulless.<br /> \u200bForce them to watch Disney films until their minds liquefy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:17:31-08:00","id":1038753,"title":"","content":"I've been going through Sanctum &amp; Sigil too, and it really seems like mages don't have much of a problem killing each other. And that's just regular mages, not Scelesti. If they were really concerned with the deaths feeding the Abyss they could destroy or otherwise remove their souls beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:37:24-08:00","id":1038759,"title":"","content":"There are two factors that can be for the lowering sentance:<br /> 1. They were all Free Council mages. London Consilium is run by majority of Guardians and local Gaurdians and Libertines from times of Nameless War were always on constant conflict. ( Street war was very rare, but surely political one. ) Two years prior ( because of PCs actions ) local Pentacle had been made whole like in the rest of the world. If Libertines mages were captured by only Diamond Sentinels and will be executed by almost Diamond run Council ( only one Councilor is Libertine now ), there <i>will</i> be civil unrest. MASSIVE civil unrest. With extremist like <i>Guy Fawkes Precedent</i> ( basically, local Awakened Anonymous column, see <b>Shadows of UK</b> ), we can see return of Nameless War here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> / By setting standards, Free Council is at least twice numerous than <i>whole</i> Diamond in it's numbers in the City, not to mentioned Guardians in it. /<br /> <br /> 2. On the 'arrest', one of non-Scelesti Children of Stars member was trying to stop Sentinels from killing cult leader, as she was his friend. Friend that hold him in the dark and when started hole thing with Acamoth, trapped him in Time Lock, but he still tried to stop Sentinels from killing her. What would be his punishment level, as he clearly is not Scelestus, only helped one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:44:21-08:00","id":1038760,"title":"","content":"Checked 2E corebook and found sum up on the matter of Left-Handed mages and Lex Magica:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw, p. 69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consilia also take action against Left-Handed mages. While the exact definition varies from Consilium to Consilium, a mage is frequently regarded as Left-Handed if her Obsessions or magical practices involve the abuse or destruction of souls, the destruction of the world\u2019s magical potential, routine interference with a Sleeper\u2019s Awakening, the cavalier abuse of Sleepers, Abyssal corruption, contact with the Lower Depths, or the evasion of death by extraordinary and ethically questionable deeds.<br /> <br /> When a Consilium finds a mage guilty of a crime against the Lex Magica, it levies one of several punishments. Lesser crimes merit public reprimand, payment of debts, or acts of penance on the behalf of the Consilium or wronged party. Serious crimes result in imprisonment, banishment, death, and for the most terrible crimes, death combined with the destruction of the accused\u2019s soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-27-2017, 12:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:47:18-08:00","id":1038762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1038742#post1038742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game as written seems limited to exile or execution, but if you want nothing says your table can't have a different answer.<br /> \u200bSend them to Tokyo and park their butts in an Ansho.<br /> \u200bDeath of Personality, use a secret Mind ritual to strip out the parts of their personalities the Pentacle finds unacceptable.<br /> \u200bAn Artifact or device that allows you to lock away the part of their soul that connects to the Supernal without completely severing its link to the individual and leaving them soulless.<br /> \u200bForce them to watch Disney films until their minds liquefy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, especially Death of Personality. But do not Scelesti contacts with Abyss corrupts <i>their</i> souls? Because if yes, then Mind Reprogramming will not erase their past as Abyssal worshipers, it would only infect their new lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T22:15:21-08:00","id":1038769,"title":"","content":"If the punishment is death, kill them expediently. If the punishment is annihilation, take them to the edge of the Ocean Ouroboros and shove them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T23:04:29-08:00","id":1038773,"title":"","content":"Side question - Are there ready in-setting precedents of rulings? Like 'In the year XYZS he destroyed utterly soul of Scelestus ABC because of him summoning...'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T00:16:11-08:00","id":1038788,"title":"","content":"On the FC/Consilium divide, there's nothing preventing a negotiation with the FC about how to proceed with the trial so the FC won't feel shut out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T01:47:12-08:00","id":1038804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1038762#post1038762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, especially Death of Personality. But do not Scelesti contacts with Abyss corrupts <i>their</i> souls? Because if yes, then Mind Reprogramming will not erase their past as Abyssal worshipers, it would only infect their new lives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You could attempt to to perform something equivalent to a lobotomy on their soul to try an cut away the infected part. But like cutting gangrene from a living host if you miss any it will just come back. That brings up another question, gangrene can cause the blood to go septic, is there such a thing as the soul going septic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-27-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T01:58:44-08:00","id":1038806,"title":"","content":"It's gangrene so you know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T02:01:31-08:00","id":1038807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1038806#post1038806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's gangrene so you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya and it is also 3 in the morning and wasn't really paying attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-27-2017, 05:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T02:31:35-08:00","id":1038814,"title":"","content":"If they are indeed proven to be Scelesti. then off with their heads. Possibly some spiritual scourging followed by life imprisonment, either by Mages or in a human prison for very serious cooperation with the Consilium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T04:00:44-08:00","id":1038826,"title":"","content":"Keep them in a time stasis, or time revert them to time from before abyssing. &quot;Send into 7 days ahead where they will be immediately sent into 7 days ahead where they will be immediately sent into 7 days ahead&quot; is also a viable tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T06:06:03-08:00","id":1038855,"title":"","content":"Is it still <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-%E2%80%8B-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists\">these mages</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:03:11-08:00","id":1038898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1038855#post1038855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it still <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980165-%E2%80%8B-2e-fight-fire-with-fire-running-awakened-antagonists&quot;]these</a> mages[/URL]?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's those.<br /> <br /> I feel that 'ripping their souls and letting live as lunatcis' would be Civitas answer. More reasonable and empathic Counsiliors would probably be after quick death, as it's shoetening their pain. ( Like killing sick cattle or horse. ) I supposw that Free Council and Silver Ladder Consiliours would be after trying Psychic Reprogramming and 'soul surgery' on Scelesti - then banishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:20:10-08:00","id":1038910,"title":"","content":"I think they'd be more likely to kill them. Even your quote above said that. Banishment wouldn't really help the problem if they were trying to summon an acamoth. What's to keep them from doing it outside the city?<br /> <br /> The fiction for the Silver Ladder's entry to the third chapter has a trial where a soul is on the line. It also seems to be the only punishment available when a Lictor goes corrupt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-27-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:00:06-08:00","id":1038931,"title":"","content":"There's nothing empathic about ripping out a person's soul and letting them live as basically zombies with irreparable mental damage. Civitas, being a Guardian, would kill them and thus give them another chance on the Diamond Wheel as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> The SL would probably agree with the Guardians on this one.<br /> <br /> The FC, it depends, who were they hurting more? Because if they directed their damage at just the Seers then they were fighting the followers of the Lie. If not though, hey, FC will kill people if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 01-27-2017, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:23:03-08:00","id":1039103,"title":"","content":"Players stated they will try to convince Ruling Council to not kill Scelesti - so there is this. Free Council would pitty Scelesti, as they become them simply by going with thei Techne and nor sinister Obsessions - remember that King in Yellow <b>makes</b> you worship him. And Silver Ladder are most humanist of Orders - they build whole Lex Magica too NOT KILL mages in first place. Rest of Orders - with Guardians and Arrows lead - would vote for the clean kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T14:29:09-08:00","id":1039110,"title":"","content":"The Lex allows for and even calls for capital punishment in some cases. Just because it was created as a means of arbitration doesn't mean that the Silver Ladder is suddenly against killing criminals who serve the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The FC might be sympathetic, but that doesn't mean they'd let the Scelesti off the death penalty either. &quot;Going with their Techne&quot; is not an excuse for surrendering to the Abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T21:48:32-08:00","id":1039253,"title":"","content":"Both Free Council and Silver Ladder Councilors are Mind Masters ( Dreamspeaker and Clavicularius precisely ) - if any one can believe 'we can fix them with Mind Arcanum', it's those guys. Still, Guardians majority will almost ensure death of Scelesti. ( If PC will not crush oponent factotum in debate. Probably will run trial as Social Chase from <b>CoD Rulebook</b> with HUGE penalties to defended to save Scelesti from dying. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T00:34:04-08:00","id":1039299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mind can totally fix their screwed up souls and scrub the permanent connection to the Abyss they've created via their legacy. /s","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T01:56:23-08:00","id":1039316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1039299#post1039299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Mind can totally fix their screwed up souls and scrub the permanent connection to the Abyss they've created via their legacy. /s</div> </div> </div> </div>Children of the Stars Legacy is <i>nowhere near</i> Abyss. It's base on communicating with Oracles in form of 'Ancient Aliens'. King in Yellow just used their curiosity to look for their First Ones in Astral domains. As to souls connection to Abyss - I think that Prime Master spells should be able to cleanse it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T02:01:10-08:00","id":1039317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1038773#post1038773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Side question - Are there ready in-setting precedents of rulings? Like 'In the year XYZS he destroyed utterly soul of Scelestus ABC because of him summoning...'</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. Do you, as the ST, say there are?<br /> <br /> CofD is not as absolute in it's setting as WoD is. If you declare that there are precedents, there are. If you declare that there aren't, there aren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:05:36-08:00","id":1039334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1038545-left-handed-and-lex-magica?p=1039317#post1039317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends. Do you, as the ST, say there are?<br /> <br /> CofD is not as absolute in it's setting as WoD is. If you declare that there are precedents, there are. If you declare that there aren't, there aren't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's obvious, but I ask is something proposed in books? In <b>Sanctum &amp; Sigil</b> we have mentioned few Illuminations, but nothing of magnitude like Scelesti or any Left-Handed trial.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T10:20:18-08:00","id":1039481,"title":"","content":"From Left-Hand Path, p17-18, 'Of the punishments levied to the Left-Handed, exile and death are the most common. Imprisonment is usually only used for mages who haven\u2019t yet shaped their souls into a tainted Legacy, those who can be reformed with work and are capable of not relapsing. Even then, the resources needed to keep a mage against his will are so great that imprisonment is reserved for convicts who successfully plead for it and prove they intend to reform. The only sure way to prevent a mage from using magic (as part of imprisonment or as its own punishment) is to remove his soul, which drives the victim insane after too long. For this reason, only mages who can be trusted to stick to their conditions of arrest are imprisoned for any length of time. That leaves exile, mundane execution, and execution combined with the destruction of the convict\u2019s soul, with increasing levels of severity as predicated by the crimes committed and the appetite of the Consilium to commit murder or soul-crime themselves. When capital punishment is used, the Guardians volunteer one of their own as the \u201cInterfector,\u201d the Consilum\u2019s headsman, who risks his own Wisdom for the good of all.'<br /> <br /> Clearly you want to avoid execution and use reform. That's the story you want, so you should go with that way. You know the characters better than us, but you could just have them willing to spend the resources to try and rehabilitate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T15:11:27-08:00","id":1039621,"title":"","content":"Well, it was not quite my own story to tell, but <u>players</u> - they decided ( after very cool and deep long debate ) that they think that morally killing Children of the Stars simply by being 'infected' with King in Yellow was not <i>just</i>. More, they think that they can cure them, with Masters of Mind and Prime in local society. And we run Social Chase as Consilium Trial, that they massively won ( on part as players got great rolls and NPC offender get terrible rolls, but more as players preparation and real surprising me ). So yes, PCs shown that in this particular case Left-Handed can be cure and rehabilitated. Whole trial ended with sentencing Children of Stars cabal on public works after psychic reprogramming and Abyss corruption cleansing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-28-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T16:15:01-08:00","id":1039656,"title":"","content":"There is a way to make people lose their magic, actually - force them to create enough Soul Stones that their maximum gnosis drops to 0. Then, if you want to reform them, suggest a Mystery revolving around cleansing the Soul Stones in some way and when they are pure, reintegrating them into Children.<br /> Obviously this is pure fantasy on my point, but it sounds appropriate.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Actually, I really like this idea - both as a soul-surgery for removing stuff like unwanted Legacies or Abyssal Taint, and as a way to punish Mages who are ruled unworthy of their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-28-2017, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}